The walker is a two-dimensional bipedal robot consisting of seven main body parts - a single torso at the top (with the two legs splitting after the torso), two thighs in the middle below the torso, two legs below the thighs, and two feet attached to the legs on which the entire body rests. The goal is to walk in the forward (right) direction by applying torque to the six hinges connecting the seven body parts.

The obverstation space consists of the following 19 parts (in order):
- state[0]: z-coordinate of the torso (height of Walker2d)
- state[1]: angle of the torso
- state[2]: angle of the thigh joint
- state[3]: angle of the leg joint
- state[4]: angle of the foot joint
- state[5]: angle of the left thigh joint
- state[6]: angle of the left leg joint
- state[7]: angle of the left foot joint
- state[8]: velocity of the x-coordinate of the torso
- state[9]: velocity of the z-coordinate (height) of the torso
- state[10]: angular velocity of the angle of the torso
- state[11]: angular velocity of the thigh hinge
- state[12]: angular velocity of the leg hinge
- state[13]: angular velocity of the foot hinge
- state[14]: angular velocity of the thigh hinge
- state[15]: angular velocity of the leg hinge
- state[16]: angular velocity of the foot hinge
- state[17]: sinusoidal phase feature sin(phase), a periodic feature to help produce alternating gait
- state[18]: sinusoidal phase feature cos(phase), a periodic feature to help produce alternating gait

The action space consists of the following 6 parts (in order):
- action[0]: Torque applied on the thigh rotor
- action[1]: Torque applied on the leg rotor
- action[2]: Torque applied on the foot rotor
- action[3]: Torque applied on the left thigh rotor
- action[4]: Torque applied on the left leg rotor
- action[5]: Torque applied on the left foot rotor

{% if policy_type == "mlp" %}
The policy is a one-hidden-layer MLP with {{ rank }} parameters and hidden size {{ mlp_hidden_dim }}.
It works as follows:
h = tanh(state @ W1 + b1)
action = h @ W2 + b2
where W1 maps the 19-dimensional state to the {{ mlp_hidden_dim }}-dimensional hidden layer, and W2 maps the hidden layer to the 6-dimensional action.
The last two state dimensions are periodic phase features intended to help the policy produce repeated alternating steps.
{% else %}
The policy is a linear policy with {{ rank }} parameters and works as follows: 
action = state @ W + B
where W maps the 19-dimensional state to the 6-dimensional action, and B is a 6-dimensional bias term.
The last two state dimensions are periodic phase features intended to help the linear policy produce repeated alternating steps.
{% endif %}

The total reward is: reward = healthy_reward bonus + forward_reward - ctrl_cost.

healthy_reward: Every timestep that the Walker2d is alive, it receives a fixed reward of value healthy_reward (default is 1).
forward_reward: A reward for moving forward, this reward would be positive if the walker moves forward (in the positive direction / in the right direction). 
ctrl_cost: A negative reward to penalize the Walker2d for taking actions that are too large. 

The goal is to walk in the forward (right) direction by applying torque to the six hinges connecting the seven body parts.
